Generating a PacBio genome from raw reads

##raw reads obtained from the BYU sequencing center from one female collected August 2025. Using PacBio HiFi assembly HiFiasm from Purdue. 

Raw data is in /uufs/chpc.utah.edu/common/home/gompert-group6/data/genome_e_pallescens/
All other work being done in /uufs/chpc.utah.edu/common/home/u6047808/sandmountain_blue/ReferenceGenome/genome_e_pallescens
Downloaded hifiasm from github by cd-ing into directory and using 'make'. Put it into a bin in my home directory and used this path in my scripts when needed. 

Converted the bam to fastq file using samtools fastq with script bam2fastq.sbatch
Preliminary results on how the genome looked using hifiasm using script 

Decided to run with Hifiasm. 
Piped the .gfa to .fasta conversion via awk directly into same slurm script for all three outputs (p_ctg, hap1, hap2) so single job
confirms whether whole pipeline worked. 
Ran with sbatch hifiasm.sh
